  "transcription_notes": [
    "The article reports only objective-value summaries. It does not publish constraint violations, feasibility rates, or median-solution violation-count vectors, so feasibility of the reported AOBLMOA solutions cannot be independently established.",
    "Official CEC2020 problem IDs, dimensions, constraint counts, and dimension-derived budgets are included as source context. The article does not identify the RC numbers or state that AOBLMOA used the official evaluation budgets.",
    "The article says that the SASS, COLSHADE, and sCMAgES results come from the official CEC2020 archive. Their submitted raw objective and constraint-violation files are present there; no corresponding AOBLMOA raw files are present.",
    "Table 15 prints an AOBLMOA average and minimum of 0.032213, a maximum of 0.035048, and a standard deviation of 0.000982459. The rounded summary is preserved without attempting to reconstruct or correct the unavailable samples.",
    "Table 16 prints an sCMAgES maximum of 0.012669, while the official submitted final-objective file contains a maximum of 0.012685856. The article value is preserved because this artifact transcribes the article tables.",
    "The article describes PGTDO as six integer variables, whereas official RC22 has nine decision variables. It describes MDCBDP as having nine constraints, whereas official RC21 lists seven. The official metadata fields are not silently replaced by the article descriptions.",
    "Near-zero standard deviations are preserved exactly even when every displayed average, median, minimum, and maximum is identical at the printed precision."
  ],
  "reproduction_blockers": [
    "The article omits AOBLMOA's population size, iteration count, objective-evaluation budget, and seed schedule for Tables 14-23.",
    "The static penalty function, coefficient, constraint-violation aggregation, feasibility tolerance, and whether table values are raw objectives or penalized fitness values are not defined.",
    "The paper-linked repository contains no CEC2020 problem evaluators, constraint-handling driver, batch driver, or raw AOBLMOA outputs.",
    "The article omits the competition-required constraint-violation, feasibility-rate, and violation-count results, preventing a feasibility-aware comparison.",
    "The article's RC21/RC22 problem descriptions conflict with the official suite metadata, and the current Mayfly package does not implement all ten selected official CEC2020 constrained problems.",
    "The paper/code/library AOBLMOA fidelity conflicts recorded in aoblmoa-2023-tables5-6.json remain open."
  ],
